For example:

Supported
Repository rule exists
+
diff violates it
+
code context confirms it
Unverified
LLM thinks something is wrong
but no supporting repository rule or deterministic evidence exists
Contradicted
LLM says X
but repository documentation explicitly permits X

That makes the system much safer.

