48. The final project definition I would use
RepoMind
Repository-Aware AI Engineering Assistant for Automated PR Review, Semantic Conflict Detection, and Developer Guidance
Problem

Modern software teams spend significant time reviewing pull requests, but generic automated reviewers may lack repository-specific architectural knowledge, produce unsupported findings, and fail to identify semantic conflicts that are not visible as ordinary Git merge conflicts.

Solution

RepoMind automatically analyzes GitHub pull requests using:

repository-specific RAG
source-code context
static analysis
test results
semantic conflict analysis
LLM reasoning
evidence validation
PR risk analysis
historical review information

It then generates an explainable review report and gives the human reviewer an AI assistant for understanding findings, exploring repository architecture, and deciding whether changes are safe.

Human role

RepoMind recommends.

A human approves.

Secondary intelligence

Historical PR metadata can be used to estimate cycle time and delay risk.

Research question

Does repository-aware, evidence-grounded AI review improve PR review quality and reduce unsupported findings compared with generic LLM review and LLM + static-analysis review?

